      "confidence": 0.8,
      "curator_note": "Eq 4.19, OE+. inductive cleavage of a doubly-bonded heteroatom system R2C=Y+. -> R+ + R-C.=Y (charge migrates to the departing alkyl; complementary to alpha-cleavage which keeps the charge as R-C#Y+ acylium). Book draws 2 resonance fishhooks depicting the OE+. <-> distonic R2C(+)-Y(.) resonance (one on the left structure at Y, one inside the parenthetical form at C); it does NOT draw the fragmentation arcs. The 2 encoded moves are the implicit cleavage electron flow (both from the breaking C1-C2 sigma bond: one electron to the acyl carbon C2 giving its radical, one to Y=O3 pairing off its odd electron), not drawn as cleavage arcs on the page. Instantiated as the acetone radical cation (Y=O), O-localized charge/radical."
