      "confidence": 0.5,
      "curator_note": "Eq 4.19 is indexed to MOD rules IMS_4_19_1 (DFS [_A]1([C]2)[_A]3{=}[_A+.]4>>[_A+]1.[C]2[_A.]3{=}[_A]4, form 1) and IMS_4_19_2 (DFS [_A]1([_A]3)[C+]4{=}[_A.]2>>[_A+]1.[_A]3[C.]4{=}[_A]2, form 2). VERIFIED MISMATCH: in both DFS the central atom (map 1) is bonded to two groups on the left and leaves with ZERO bonds on the right while a NEW bond forms between its two former neighbours (2-3 in _1, 3-4 in _2). That is a detach-and-rebond (methylene-loss / 1,2-migration), not the direct cleavage of one C-R bond incident to the pi-forming carbonyl carbon that eq 4.19 depicts. The rules do not describe this scheme; see rule_mismatches."
